    id: '8',
    title: 'The Cloud That Giggled',
    content:
      "In the big blue sky lived a fluffy white cloud named Puffy.\n\nPuffy looked like a marshmallow that had learned to float.\n\nHe loved sunshine.\nHe loved breezes.\nBut most of all… Puffy loved laughing.\n\nAnd Puffy was extremely ticklish.\n\nWhen a tiny gust of wind poked his side—“Hee hee hee!”—Puffy would giggle.\n\nWhen birds flew too close—“Hahaha!”—he would shake with laughter.\n\nThe other clouds would sigh.\n\n“Puffy,” said a tall cloud named Greyson, “your giggles sound like thunder.”\n\nPuffy tried to be serious. He puffed his cheeks. He folded his cloud-arms.\n\n“I am a grown-up cloud,” he declared.\n\nRight then, an airplane zoomed through him.\n\n*Vrrrrrrr!*\n\nPuffy squealed. “HEE HEE HEE!”\n\nThe sky rumbled.\n\nDown below, kids looked up.\n\n“Did you hear that?” one child asked.\n\n“Thunder!” another said.\n\n“No,” said a little girl, squinting. “It sounds like… a laugh.”\n\nPuffy tried to stop. Truly. He wanted to be helpful and calm.\n\nBut then something magical happened.\n\nA rainbow appeared.\n\nNot a normal rainbow.\n\nThis rainbow was sneaky.\n\nIt floated close and gently brushed Puffy’s belly with its red stripe.\n\nPuffy’s eyes widened.\n\n“No,” he whispered.\n\nThe orange stripe tickled too.\n\n“Noooo,” Puffy whispered again.\n\nThen the yellow stripe tickled like a feather.\n\nPuffy exploded into laughter.\n\n“BAHAHAHAHA!”\n\nHis whole cloud-body shook.\n\nAnd as he laughed, tiny raindrops popped out like sparkling beads.\n\nThe sun shone through those raindrops.\n\nSuddenly, it looked like the sky was raining glitter.\n\nDown below, the kids squealed.\n\n“It’s raining sunshine!” they shouted.\n\nThey ran outside, spinning and dancing, catching raindrops on their tongues.\n\nPuffy’s laughter softened into happy chuckles.\n\nHe watched the kids play and felt proud.\n\nGreyson drifted beside him. “Well,” Greyson admitted, “your giggles are not so bad. They made the children smile.”\n\nPuffy beamed. “Maybe laughter is a kind of weather,” he said.\n\nGreyson raised an eyebrow. “Weather?”\n\n“Yes!” Puffy said. “Sometimes people need sunshine. Sometimes they need rain. And sometimes… they need a little laughing-thunder to shake the sadness away.”\n\nThat night, as the sky turned purple, Puffy decided to practice.\n\nHe tried a gentle giggle.\n\n“Heh heh.”\n\nA tiny sprinkle fell.\n\nBelow, one child looked up from the window and smiled.\n\nPuffy sighed happily.\n\nHe was still ticklish.\n\nStill giggly.\n\nAnd now he knew his laughter could be a gift—sprinkling joy where it was needed most.",
